[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3550583490","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112934#issuecomment-3550583490","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112934","id":3550583490,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7ToZrC","user":{"login":"fire","id":32321,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMzIx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32321?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire","html_url":"https://github.com/fire","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-19T03:49:37Z","updated_at":"2025-11-19T03:49:37Z","body":"Is there an inverse tonemap operator we can use?","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3550583490/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3550597865","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112934#issuecomment-3550597865","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112934","id":3550597865,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7TodLp","user":{"login":"allenwp","id":17506573,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NTA2NTcz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17506573?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp","html_url":"https://github.com/allenwp","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-19T03:59:03Z","updated_at":"2025-11-19T03:59:03Z","body":"> Is there an inverse tonemap operator we can use?\n\nNo, the tonemappers are not designed to be easily inverted.\n\nBut I suspect this bug is caused by failing to apply the nonlinear sRGB transfer function when saving the viewport texture when HDR 2D is enabled. (When HDR 2D is enabled, the viewport texture remains linear-encoded until `blit.glsl`, where the nonlinear sRGB transfer function is applied. This is different than HDR 2D disabled, in which case the sRGB transfer function was applied as the viewport texture buffer is written to.)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3550597865/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3556154567","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112934#issuecomment-3556154567","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112934","id":3556154567,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7T9pzH","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-20T06:34:38Z","updated_at":"2025-11-20T06:34:38Z","body":"This was already fixed by https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100659\n\nSee the docs for [`get_texture()`](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/latest/classes/class_viewport.html#class-viewport-method-get-texture). \n\n> Note: When [use_hdr_2d](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/latest/classes/class_viewport.html#class-viewport-property-use-hdr-2d) is true the returned texture will be an HDR image using linear encoding.\n\nSince the image is linearly encoded, you need to call `Image.linear_to_srgb()` before saving if you expect the saved result to be sRGB encoded","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3556154567/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3560389010","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112934#issuecomment-3560389010","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112934","id":3560389010,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7UNzmS","user":{"login":"allenwp","id":17506573,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NTA2NTcz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17506573?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp","html_url":"https://github.com/allenwp","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-20T22:29:04Z","updated_at":"2025-11-20T22:29:04Z","body":"> This was already fixed by [#100659](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100659)\n\nHmm. I'm not sure how this is related.\n\n> See the docs for [`get_texture()`](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/latest/classes/class_viewport.html#class-viewport-method-get-texture).\n> \n> > Note: When [use_hdr_2d](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/latest/classes/class_viewport.html#class-viewport-property-use-hdr-2d) is true the returned texture will be an HDR image using linear encoding.\n> \n> Since the image is linearly encoded, you need to call `Image.linear_to_srgb()` before saving if you expect the saved result to be sRGB encoded\n\nIf I'm understanding correctly, this would mean the following script would resolve the issue:\n\n```\nvar image := get_tree().root.get_viewport().get_texture().get_image()\nimage.linear_to_srgb()\nimage.save_jpg(folder_path + \"jpg.jpg\")\n```\n\nBut `Image.linear_to_srgb()` is only available for RGB8 textures:\n```\nE 0:00:00:447   node_3d.gd:11 @ _ready(): Condition \"format != FORMAT_RGB8 && format != FORMAT_RGBA8\" is true.\n  <C++ Source>  core/io/image.cpp:4195 @ linear_to_srgb()\n  <Stack Trace> node_3d.gd:11 @ _ready()\n```\n\nBecause `Image` is aware of its format(?), I would expect it to be able to interpret its data and correctly save to all formats by using the appropriate encoding transformations...","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3560389010/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4529535724","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112934#issuecomment-4529535724","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112934","id":4529535724,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABDfs67A","user":{"login":"VitSoonYoung","id":89907596,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5OTA3NTk2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/89907596?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/VitSoonYoung","html_url":"https://github.com/VitSoonYoung","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VitSoonYoung/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VitSoonYoung/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VitSoonYoung/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VitSoonYoung/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VitSoonYoung/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VitSoonYoung/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VitSoonYoung/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VitSoonYoung/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VitSoonYoung/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-24T17:54:35Z","updated_at":"2026-05-24T17:54:35Z","body":"For anyone reading this problem, here is a work around I spend 30 minutes fighting it:\n\n```python\n\tvar image := get_viewport().get_texture().get_image()\n\n\tif get_viewport().use_hdr_2d:\n\t\tif image.get_format() != Image.FORMAT_RGB8:\n\t\t\timage.convert(Image.FORMAT_RGB8)\n\t\timage.linear_to_srgb()\n\n       image.save_png(path)\n```\n\nI don't know what these do, I just know it worked","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4529535724/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4537770087","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112934#issuecomment-4537770087","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112934","id":4537770087,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABDnjgZw","user":{"login":"allenwp","id":17506573,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NTA2NTcz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17506573?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp","html_url":"https://github.com/allenwp","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-25T22:48:49Z","updated_at":"2026-05-25T22:48:49Z","body":"Thanks for sharing. This is the best approach for Godot 4.7 and earlier, but you may notice a loss of detail in darker or saturated colours in the image that causes banding to appear in gradients. This issue is resolved by https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119093 which removes the need to convert the linear-encoded colours  to `FORMAT_RGB8` before using `linear_to_srgb()`.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4537770087/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5628895470","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112934#issuecomment-5628895470","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112934","id":5628895470,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABT4Ig7g","user":{"login":"allenwp","id":17506573,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NTA2NTcz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17506573?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp","html_url":"https://github.com/allenwp","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-11T03:13:47Z","updated_at":"2026-09-11T03:13:47Z","body":"This issue has been resolved by #119093. Now all that's needed to avoid a dark image is the following:\n\n``` gdscript\nvar image := get_viewport().get_texture().get_image()\nif get_viewport().use_hdr_2d:\n\timage.linear_to_srgb()\nimage.save_jpg(folder_path + \"jpg.jpg\")\n```\n\nIt might be nice if `Image` had some sort of metadata that indicated its colour encoding such that the `save_` functions would work automatically without the user needing to make an extra function call to `linear_to_srgb()`. This could be possible, since the `Viewport` knows about its encoding, but `Texture` doesn't, so maybe a new API would be needed to get an `Image` directly from the `Viewport`, which seems like bloat for a small convenience like this. So the state things are now in are probably the best they will be for Godot 4.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5628895470/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]